<title>NEW ZEALAND: New Zealand scraps alcohol excise review.</title>
<headline>New Zealand scraps alcohol excise review.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government has scrapped a review of the alcohol excise, Treasurer Winston Peters told parliament in answer to a written question.</p>
<p>Asked by Labour MP Rick Barker whether he intended to reconvene the multi-party committee initiated during the passing of the Customs and Excise Act in 1996, Peters said: &quot;No. Cabinet has agreed not to proceed with a review of the alcohol excise.&quot; The review was established after pressure from former Conservative MP Trevor Rogers, who wanted to see the tax reduced.</p>
</text>
